## Component Documentation

### ModelLifecycle
The main container component for model deployment and improvement documentation.

### DeploymentPhase
Represents the initial deployment phase of a model.

Props:
- `title`: string - The phase title
- `type`: 'initialization' | 'enhancement' | 'maintenance' - The type of phase
- `description`: string - A brief description of the phase

### DeploymentStep
Represents a specific step in the deployment process.

Props:
- `step`: string - The step description
- `type`: 'configuration' | 'infrastructure' | 'tokenization' - The type of step
- `importance`: 'high' | 'medium' | 'low' - The importance level
- `description`: string - A brief description of the step
- `order`: number - The sequential order of the step

### ImprovementPhase
Represents the model improvement phase.

Props:
- `title`: string - The phase title
- `type`: 'enhancement' | 'maintenance' | 'optimization' - The type of phase
- `description`: string - A brief description of the phase

### ImprovementStep
Represents a specific step in the improvement process.

Props:
- `step`: string - The step description
- `type`: 'contribution' | 'validation' | 'reward' - The type of step
- `importance`: 'high' | 'medium' | 'low' - The importance level
- `description`: string - A brief description of the step
- `order`: number - The sequential order of the step

## Usage Example

```tsx
<ModelLifecycle>
  <DeploymentPhase
    title="Example Phase"
    type="initialization"
    description="Example deployment phase"
  >
    <DeploymentStep
      step="Example step"
      type="configuration"
      importance="high"
      description="Example step description"
      order={1}
    />
  </DeploymentPhase>
</ModelLifecycle>
```

## Notes
- Each phase should have clear entry and exit criteria
- Steps should be performed in the specified order
- Document all performance metrics and their calculation methods
- Include validation requirements for each step
- Specify token distribution rules
- Document quality assurance procedures
- Include rollback procedures for failed deployments
- Specify monitoring and maintenance requirements
